> sources --- beside the cores' own; so an atom's own birth and its cores' births are separate facts. The same holds for every result, not Collapse alone: a result is a new atom with its own new $V_{\text{timestamp}}$ and a backward $V_{\text{link}}$ naming its operands, and the cores that survive into it keep theirs. A result is, for these purposes, one new core on top of the cores it keeps: besides its timestamp and backward link it carries its own $V_{\text{derived}}$, the sum of everything it holds, and it may carry its own $V_{\text{location}}$ and $V_{\text{expiry}}$ where a use supplies them; absent means absent. Collapse destroys none of the cores' meta vectors, and no verb computes a location or an expiry for a result from those of its operands.
