> \paragraph{The meta-vector catalogue.} All meta vectors are uncapped. A scalar kind takes one axis, $\mathbb{R}^1$; a kind of two angles takes a plane, $\mathbb{R}^2$; each lives in its own space or in axes disjoint from the content's. The entries are recommendations of the same standing as the dictionaries, so that meta vectors from different sources line up; a use may choose another unit if it states it.
> \begin{center}
> \small
> \begin{tabular}{@{}p{2.5cm}p{3.3cm}p{3.6cm}p{3.7cm}@{}}
> \hline
> Kind & Space & Unit & Compared by \\ \hline
> $V_{\text{timestamp}}$, $V_{\text{expiry}}$ & $\mathbb{R}^1$, one axis each & seconds since 1970-01-01 00:00 UTC & difference of values \\
> clock face & $\mathbb{R}^2$: minute on $\phi$, hour on $\chi$, $\theta$ at the equator & angle & cyclic distance \\
> $V_{\text{location}}$ & $\mathbb{R}^2$: polar angle, azimuth & angle & great-circle distance \\
> $V_{\text{derived}}$ & $\mathbb{R}^{N_{\mathrm{dim}}}$ & strength & vector distance \\
> seat $\vec P$ & $\mathbb{R}^3$ & a length the use chooses & Euclidean distance \\
> $V_{\text{link}}$ & $\mathbb{R}^1$, an identifier & none & equality \\
> $V_{\text{identity}}$ & the tuple (sort, link, timestamp) of meta vectors the core already carries; no axis of its own & none & equality; never enters the equality of atoms \\
> $V_{\text{container}}$ & $\mathbb{R}^1$ per vector: the position of its core & an index & equality; \emph{enters} the equality of atoms, being the grouping itself, so it is listed here beside the meta vectors and is not one in the strict sense \\ \hline
> \end{tabular}
> \end{center}
